{"h":3406,"lines":[{"x":0.90305906950756765,"h":0.014682657216061434,"w":0.063984953562418623,"c":1,"y":0.042077275737835262,"t":"Test 1"},{"t":"SECTION 4","h":0.015988371754420583,"y":0.088662790854863394,"w":0.16082473754882812,"x":0.074226806395845224,"c":1},{"y":0.11773255818964734,"w":0.76494847615559891,"h":0.014680829946951413,"c":1,"x":0.070103081406174772,"t":"Ive been looking at ocean biodiversity, that's the diversity of species that live in the world's"},{"c":1,"w":0.7587628682454427,"t":"oceans. About 20 years ago biologists developed the idea of what they called 'biodiversity","x":0.070103101875776591,"y":0.13358778603574151,"h":0.014679976512037562},{"w":0.77113403320312501,"x":0.072164942066873822,"h":0.014534883616744709,"t":"hotspots'. These are the areas which have the greatest mixture of species, so one example","y":0.14970930237549829,"c":1},{"w":0.77537322998046876,"x":0.072102374114012949,"h":0.017264773267475997,"t":"is Madagascar. Ihese hotspots are significant because they allow us to locate key areas for","y":0.16471474805023989,"c":1},{"x":0.87422680370321737,"w":0.037113402684529673,"c":1,"y":0.16715116268710717,"t":"Q31","h":0.013081395479068947},{"x":0.070103082772947314,"t":"focusing efforts at conservation. Biologists can identify hotspots on land, fairly easily, but until","y":0.18168604667767951,"w":0.78762888590494795,"h":0.015988371754420694,"c":1},{"t":"recently, very little was known about species distribution and diversity in the oceans, and no","x":0.070044273895302919,"h":0.018895246110379738,"y":0.19638350258851811,"w":0.77536727905273439,"c":1},{"t":"one even knew if hotspots existed there.","x":0.072037036387575498,"y":0.21244488780147996,"w":0.34259529113769527,"h":0.015824773769412381,"c":1},{"x":0.074172056768463321,"h":0.01564139782227425,"w":0.76298797607421875,"y":0.2363350774214299,"c":1,"t":"Then a Canadian biologist called Boris Worm did some research in 2005 on data on ocean"},{"c":1,"w":0.74226801554361976,"y":0.25425719338124309,"t":"species that he got from the fishing industry. Worm located five hotspots for large ocean","x":0.070103105522004508,"h":0.014679976512037562},{"c":1,"y":0.27034883737639537,"t":"predators like sharks, and looked at what they had in common. The main thing he'd expected. Q32","x":0.070103083517264797,"w":0.84123713175455717,"h":0.015988371754420583},{"t":"to find was that they had very high concentrations of food, but to his surorise that was only","h":0.016147974163241319,"x":0.068041242276934213,"c":1,"w":0.76907216389973965,"y":0.28479154436899301},{"x":0.068041239478466478,"w":0.76082473754882807,"c":1,"h":0.01453488361674482,"y":0.30232558144316657,"t":"true for four of the hotspots - the remaining hotspot was quite badly orf in that regard. But"},{"y":0.31826189076180222,"h":0.016147974163241319,"t":"what he did find was that in all cases, the water at the surface of the ocean had relatively.","w":0.76288660685221354,"c":1,"x":0.068041232734083607},{"y":0.3343023256288884,"t":"high temperatures, even when it was cool at greater depths, so this seemed to be a factor in","c":1,"w":0.77938145955403648,"h":0.01453488361674482,"x":0.070103084689900758},{"h":0.016147974163241319,"t":"supporting a diverse range of these large predators. However, this wasn't enough on its own,","x":0.068041245662199878,"y":0.35026423967894238,"c":1,"w":0.7896907043457031},{"t":"because he also found that the water needed to have enough oxygen in it - so these two","x":0.070103097943996981,"y":0.36627906968052359,"h":0.013081395479068947,"w":0.75257731119791671,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.67628865559895834,"h":0.015989225189334433,"t":"factors seemed necessary to support the high metabolic rate of these large fish.","x":0.068041239103455484,"y":0.38226658859229856},{"c":1,"x":0.070103088754756585,"t":"A couple of years later, in 2007, a researcher called Lisa Ballance, who was working in","w":0.73195877075195315,"h":0.016147974163241319,"y":0.40692894863772011},{"x":0.070103111743935922,"y":0.42151162797546338,"w":0.78556696573893237,"t":"California, also started looking for ocean hotspots, but not for fish - what she was interested.","h":0.017441859892096456,"c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.013081395479069058,"y":0.42296511617547916,"t":"Q35","x":0.87216494916982323,"w":0.039175256093343047},{"c":1,"h":0.014679976512037562,"t":"in was marine mammals, things like seals. And she found three places in the oceans which","x":0.068041237459733186,"w":0.76907216389973954,"y":0.43893129743307235},{"h":0.016434925413103763,"c":1,"x":0.070043055333708637,"t":"were hotspots, and what these had in common was that these hotspots were all located at","w":0.76301839192708343,"y":0.45344176153198057},{"t":"boundaries between ocean currents, and this seems to be the sort of place that has lots of","c":1,"w":0.76701029459635417,"x":0.068041244431710002,"y":0.47093023260675504,"h":0.01453488361674482},{"c":1,"w":0.41649485270182296,"y":0.48678802120026932,"h":0.013211978860833806,"t":"the plankton that some of these species feed on.","x":0.070103089010545711},{"w":0.75463918050130208,"h":0.013081395479068947,"c":1,"t":"So now people who want to protect the species that are endangered need to get as much","x":0.072164945728163912,"y":0.5116279069098314},{"w":0.76092732747395841,"c":1,"x":0.067982057480811681,"y":0.52600567101255147,"h":0.017101342721469903,"t":"information as possible. For example, there's an international project called the Census of"},{"c":1,"t":"Marine Life. They've been surveying oceans all over the world, including the Arctic. One","x":0.070103080092557099,"y":0.54215116295768184,"w":0.74226806640624998,"h":0.015988371754420583},{"y":0.5436046510613376,"h":0.013081395479068947,"t":"Q36","x":0.87010309350544746,"w":0.039175256093343158,"c":1},{"w":0.77546905517578124,"x":0.06795191058234612,"y":0.55531146483446703,"h":0.018855831305279236,"t":"thing they found there which stunned other researchers was that there were large numbers","c":1},{"y":0.57398708186555081,"w":0.76701029459635417,"h":0.014679976512037674,"c":1,"t":"of species which live below the ice - sometimes under a layer up to 20 metres thick. Some","x":0.068041244369457562},{"t":"of these species had never been seen before. They've even found species of octopus living","h":0.016136292072862823,"x":0.067998605307005841,"y":0.58999011757381448,"w":0.77330006917317706,"c":1},{"t":"in these conditions. And other scientists working on the same project, but researching very","x":0.070103081396335559,"y":0.60745742798803526,"w":0.76494847615559891,"h":0.013211978860833806,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"different habitats on the ocean floor, have found large numbers of species congregating","x":0.065932477258326877,"w":0.74237904866536464,"h":0.018785049967113387,"y":0.621570057750226},{"w":0.6041236877441406,"c":1,"x":0.068041248810403937,"y":0.63945977701772816,"t":"around volcanoes, attracted to them by the warmth and nutrients there.","h":0.014679976512037562},{"w":0.71340204874674473,"c":1,"t":"However, biologists still don't know how serious the threat to their survival is for each","x":0.070103099235175534,"y":0.68750000016697066,"h":0.015988371754420583},{"x":0.068041249331830228,"t":"individual species. So a body called the Global Marine Species Assessment is now creating","y":0.70346447428549819,"w":0.77319585164388027,"h":0.014679976512037562,"c":1},{"x":0.068041225735754829,"y":0.71947674423607455,"w":0.76494847615559891,"t":"a list of endangered species on land, so they consider things like the size of the population","h":0.01453488361674482,"c":1},{"x":0.070103093207041334,"t":"- how many members of one species there are in a particular place - and then they look at","y":0.73546511621215194,"h":0.013213685730661395,"c":1,"w":0.76907216389973954},{"x":0.068041262953463785,"h":0.016001174398120876,"y":0.74999999996944666,"t":"their distribution in geographical terms, although this is quite difficult when you're looking at","c":1,"w":0.77113398234049479},{"t":"fish, because they're so mobile, and then thirdly they calculate the rate at which the decline of Q37","h":0.018439629465708984,"c":1,"x":0.067989462014976798,"y":0.76558288602585722,"w":0.8413480122884115},{"y":0.78247179625457086,"w":0.21682601928710937,"x":0.065851929163122144,"h":0.015598199679721314,"c":1,"t":"the species is happening."},{"h":0.015988371754420583,"t":"So far only 1,500 species have been assessed, but they want to increase this figure to","y":0.80668604667844657,"w":0.72989690144856767,"c":1,"x":0.068041239884667939},{"y":0.82228637279095396,"t":"20,000. For each one they assess. they use the data they collect on that species to produce.","c":1,"x":0.067994986068715665,"h":0.017885319569218683,"w":0.78563578287760416},{"h":0.013081395479069058,"y":0.822674418503198,"w":0.041237112681070887,"t":"Q38","c":1,"x":0.86597938171215638},{"y":0.83734715685468353,"w":0.77541992187499997,"c":1,"h":0.018719124920005603,"t":"a map showing its distribution. Ultimately they will be able to use these to figure out not only","x":0.067955053075407834},{"t":"where most species are located but also where they are most threatened.","h":0.013081395479068947,"x":0.068041245167233436,"c":1,"w":0.62061854044596354,"y":0.85465116272271313},{"c":1,"x":0.068041225734929475,"t":"So finally, what can be done to retain the diversity of species in the world's oceans? Firstly,","y":0.87933059326439666,"w":0.76494847615559902,"h":0.014679976512037562},{"x":0.070051188485429253,"w":0.77741165161132819,"c":1,"t":"we need to set up more reserves in our oceans, places where marine species are protected.","y":0.89496167622870604,"h":0.015956408264912736},{"h":0.014679976512037562,"w":0.77938140869140626,"c":1,"x":0.068041249949829699,"y":0.91133294193760128,"t":"We have some, but not enough. In addition, to preserve species such as leatherback turtles,"},{"t":"leltsresources.org","y":0.95282647562327316,"c":1,"x":0.35215562236188863,"h":0.024119858173363595,"w":0.29356600443522135},{"w":0.039175256093343158,"x":0.91958762958792173,"t":"107","c":1,"y":0.94622093024427623,"h":0.01453488361674482}],"w":2400}